<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  org.aquariusos.rememberdrive.policy — "remember this inside drive"
  ===========================================================================
  PLAIN ENGLISH

  This file tells polkit — the part of Linux that decides who may do what —
  that AquariusOS has one new privileged job, and what to ask before doing it.

  The job is: write one line into /etc/fstab so that a drive living INSIDE this
  computer opens by itself at every login, instead of asking for a password
  every time. The program that does it is
  /usr/libexec/aquarius-remember-drive, and it refuses, by itself, to touch the
  disk the operating system is on, the EFI partition, swap, or Windows' own
  volume.

  THE ANSWER BELOW IS "ASK FOR AN ADMINISTRATOR PASSWORD, THEN REMEMBER IT FOR
  A FEW MINUTES" (auth_admin_keep). Two reasons:

    * it is the same answer every other "this changes the whole computer"
      moment on AquariusOS gives, so nothing new has to be learned, and
    * a machine with three inside drives asks once rather than three times,
      because the person is answering three prompts in the same minute.

  The "keep" lasts only as long as polkit's own short window and never survives
  a reboot. Nothing here grants a standing permission.

  Who may answer at all is narrowed further in
  /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/50-aquarius-remember-drive.rules: the person at
  this screen, in the active local session, in the `wheel` group. Over SSH, the
  answer is simply no.

  ⚠️ This file has NOTHING to do with
  /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/49-aquarius-udisks.rules and must never be used
  as a reason to widen it. That rule stays exactly as narrow as it is: this
  feature exists so it does not have to change.
  ===========================================================================
-->
<policyconfig>

  <vendor>AquariusOS</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/stoneharborent</vendor_url>

  <action id="org.aquariusos.rememberdrive.manage">
    <description>Remember a drive inside this computer</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to open this drive at every login</message>
    <icon_name>drive-harddisk</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin_keep</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/libexec/aquarius-remember-drive</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
